  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The forces acting on the system are shown in the diagram<br /><br />For vertical equilibrium of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F</mi></math> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;....(i)<br /><br /><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0014128_AnsExp2_1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 169px;\" /></strong></u><br /><br />And for the vertical equilibrium of the system<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0014128_AnsExp2_2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 165px; height: 117px;\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>g</mi></math>, &nbsp;i.e., &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi></math> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ....(ii)<br /><br />Now the system will not move horizontally till<br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub></math><br /><br />i.e., &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>[</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>]</mo></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />which on simplification gives<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mi>T</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">g</mtext></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math><br /><br />So in the light of equation (i), we get<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">g</mtext></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math>",
